{"id": "EUVD-2026-102344", "enisaUuid": "5eac8a85-dc8a-3116-b989-76fad29eb18e", "description": "Netgate pfSense CE 2.3.0 through 2.9.0 contains a stored cross-site scripting vulnerability that allows authenticated users with Firewall: Rules or NAT: Port Forward privileges to inject scripts via the separator color field. Attackers can submit a crafted separator[] color value that display_separator() renders unencoded into class attributes, executing in administrators' browsers to perform WebGUI actions with their privileges.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:46:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T01:11:30", "baseScore": 4.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:P/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/abraxas/pfsense-separator-color-xss", "https://abraxaslabs.tech/research/pfsense-ce-leftovers", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/etc/inc/filter.inc#L6238-L6252", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/usr/local/www/firewall_rules.php#L236-L245", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/netgate-pfsense-ce-2.3.0-through-2.9.0-stored-xss-via-separator-color"], "aliases": ["GHSA-3vw7-4qg6-g75v", "CVE-2026-111232"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 1.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "52e11b1e-adec-31e9-9c53-fea027d1d807", "product": {"name": "pfSense CE", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}, "product_version": "2.3.0 \u22642.9.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c2a045cb-6890-3c70-b0c9-fe4bfd6ed788", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}], "isExploited": false}